{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/valentinakoniukhova/.agents/skills/agent-reach/references/search.md'","aggregated_output":"# 搜索工具\n\nExa AI 搜索引擎。\n\n## Exa AI 搜索\n\n高质量 AI 搜索引擎，适合查找技术文档、官方示例和相关网页。\n\n```bash\nmcporter call exa.web_search_exa query=\"query\" numResults=5\nmcporter call exa.web_search_exa query=\"library API code example\" numResults=5\n```\n\n### 使用场景\n\n| 场景 | 参数 |\n|-----|------|\n| 网页搜索 | `web_search_exa(query: \"...\", numResults: 5)` |\n| 技术/代码资料 | `web_search_exa(query: \"框架名 API 示例\", numResults: 5)` |\n\n> Exa MCP 的 `get_code_context_exa` 已弃用且默认不注册。代码问题也使用\n> `web_search_exa`；需要精确搜索仓库内容时，改用 `dev.md` 中的 GitHub 搜索。\n\n### 特点\n\n- 擅长英文内容和技术文档\n- 可通过查询词定位官方文档和代码示例\n- 结果质量高\n\n## 与其他搜索工具对比\n\n| 工具 | 来源 | 适用场景 |\n|-----|------|---------|\n| Exa | agent-reach | 英文/技术/代码搜索 |\n| 智谱搜索 | my-mcp-tools | 中文搜索 |\n| GitHub 搜索 | agent-reach (dev.md) | 仓库/代码搜索 |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"curl -Ls --max-time 15 'https://r.jina.ai/https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609' | head -100\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"curl -Ls --max-time 15 'https://r.jina.ai/https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609' | head -100\"","aggregated_output":"Title: API access to Intervals.icu - Guide - Intervals.icu Forum\n\nURL Source: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609\n\nPublished Time: 2026-10-14T18:37:49+00:00\n\nMarkdown Content:\n## post by david on 14 Oct\n\nIntervals.icu now has a public API for other applications. To use it you need to generate an API key in /settings (look for “Developer Settings” near the bottom). Your API key allows other applications to access your Intervals.icu data. Be careful what you do with it! If you suspect that your key may have been compromised immediately clear or re-generate it.\n\nBy using the API you agree to the [Intervals.icu API Terms and Conditions](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-api-terms-and-conditions/114087) .\n\nPlease not that **data from Strava is not available from the API**. Their terms and conditions do not allow it.\n\nUpdate 9th October 2026: Garmin terms and conditions have been updated and **It is likely that we will have to block access to Garmin data via the API soon**.\n\nUpdate 14th October 2026: The revisions to the agreement are part of the planned reopening of the Garmin Connect Developer Program. **There will be an easier path for individuals and apps to access data from Garmin devices**.\n\nThe API uses [basic authentication](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basic_access_authentication) for personal use. **The username is “API_KEY” and the password your API key**. Example using curl:\n\n`$ curl -u API_KEY:1l0nlqjq3j1obdhg08rz5rfhx https://intervals.icu/api/v1/athlete/2049151/activities.csv`\n\nApps intended to be used by more than one person should use [OAuth](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759) and Bearer tokens.\n\nI generated some API docs:\n\n*   [RapiDoc UI (best)](https://intervals.icu/api-docs.html)\n*   [Swagger UI (retro)](https://intervals.icu/api/v1/docs/swagger-ui/index.html)\n\nNote that you can use “0” for the athlete id for endpoints that accept an athlete id in the path. This will use the athlete for the API key or bearer token used to make the call.\n\nAlso you can [extend Intervals.icu](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/extending-intervals-icu/46565) itself using Javascript.\n\nThere are some guides for common API tasks:\n\n*   [Intervals.icu API Integration Cookbook](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-integration-cookbook/80090)\n*   [Uploading planned workouts to Intervals.icu](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/uploading-planned-workouts-to-intervals-icu/63624)\n\n## [](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609#p-1722-rate-limits-1)Rate Limits\n\nThere are limits per day (reset at midnight UTC) and per rolling 15 minute window. The following http headers are returned on each request:\n\n```\nX-RateLimit-Limit: <15m limit>,<daily limit>\nX-RateLimit-Remaining: <15m limit remaining>,<daily limit remaining>\n```\n\nOver rate limit requests receive a 429 status code and a Retry-After http header indicating how many seconds need to elapse until the call might succeed.\n\n```\nRetry-After: 370\n```\n\nThere is an additional limit of 10 calls per second per IP address. This limit does not return any rate limit related http headers.\n\nRate limits are enforced differently for API key callers and OAuth client apps.\n\n### [](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609#p-1722-oauth-client-apps-2)OAuth Client Apps\n\nThe default daily rate limit is 100/user per day up to 500 users (max 50000 requests), with a minimum of 5000. The daily limit resets at midnight UTC. Note that the per-user number is used to calculate the total daily limit and is not applied per-user, so backfills and new-user setup tasks should not be an issue.\n\nThe requests per 15 minute limit is 1/8 of the daily limit with a minimum of 2500. This is a rolling limit and does not reset at specific intervals.\n\nIf you have more than 500 users and need a higher daily limit, or a lower limit for safety, contact [support@intervals.icu](mailto:support@intervals.icu). The limits are to protect the Intervals.icu infrastructure from apps with many users suddenly generating many more calls than usual.\n\nCurrent limits and API usage information can be found on the oauth client management page (look for “Manage App” on your app on /settings/apps).\n\n### [](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609#p-1722-api-key-callers-3)API Key Callers\n\nAPI key calls are limited to 5000 requests per day and 2500 requests per rolling 15 minute window. If you need more than that you need to create an app using [OAuth](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759).\n\n## [](https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609#p-1722-cloudflare-note-4)Cloudflare Note\n\nIntervals.icu uses Cloudflare and CF considers requests from some client libraries (e.g. `Python-urllib`) to be suspicious and maybe challenge or block them. The easy fix is to change the user agent to look like a browser.\n\nread  113 min\n\n## post by Andrii_Magalich on Apr 2, 2020\n\n## post by david on Apr 3, 2020\n\n10 days later\n\n## post by david on Apr 13, 2020\n\n29 days later\n\n## post by Jules_Cusson-Fradet on May 13, 2020\n\n## post by david on May 13, 2020\n\n## post by Jules_Cusson-Fradet on May 13, 2020\n\n## post by david on May 13, 2020\n\n## post by Jules_Cusson-Fradet on May 13, 2020\n\n## post by david on May 14, 2020\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
